 "name": "Offensive Shunt",
 "type": "feat",
 "img": "modules/jjk5e/icons/techniques/teleportation.svg",
 "system": {
  "description": {
   "value": "<p><em>Prerequisite: Must have Teleport</em></p>\n<p>You have learned to use your technique offensively. When you mark an object that is Small size category or smaller, you can spend 3 CE to forcefully teleport it into a space occupied by a creature within 60 ft that you can see, which forces a Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, the object teleports into their body and they take Xd6 force damage that ignores damage resistances (X = proficiency bonus). At 6th level, you can spend additional CE up to your proficiency bonus to increase the die tier of <em>Offensive Shunt</em> by 1 per CE spent up to a maximum of d12s (d6 &gt; d8 &gt; d10 &gt; d12).<br />\n At 11th level, when teleporting a willing or unwilling creature, you can spend an additional 6 CE to teleport them into an area occupied by a Large size category object or structure or larger within 30 ft that you can see. Both the creature and the object or structure take double the damage of your <em>Offensive Shunt</em>. If this destroys the object or structure, the creature falls prone. Otherwise, the target is restrained in the item until removed or the obstruction is destroyed.</p>",
   "chat": ""
  },
